    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m having trouble using coord_map() with a large data set, although it&#39;s working fine with a smaller but otherwise similar data set. With the larger data R simply hangs when trying to create the plot. I&#39;ve pasted the code below and attached a file (large_and_small.R) containing the large and small data sets. Note that the size difference is significant. I would be inclined to write this problem off as one of the projection simply being to computationally difficult with the larger data, but another program (QGIS) can reproject the same data (as a raster layer) almost instantly on the same machine. Any idea why I&#39;m having this problem or how to solve it? Note: Using smaller data might actually be the best solution for me, but that&#39;s a separate question for another post (coming soon).<div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s how I&#39;m creating the plots and more or less what they should look like:</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">load</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;large_and_small.R&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">maps</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">RColorBrewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#800\"># Get background map</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:#000\">states_map </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> map_data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;state&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s what it should look like (except not projected):</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">states_map</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   geom_polygon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;dark grey&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   coord_map(projection=&quot;mercator&quot;, xlim=c(-125, -100), ylim=c(30, 50)) +</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   coord_cartesian</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xlim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">125</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ylim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   geom_tile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mean_large</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   scale_fill_gradientn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">colours</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">brewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;YlOrRd&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p</span></div></code></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-b1p62Zq23gk/U8lgMGSWXII/AAAAAAAAAQI/ag-CxRGgOcg/s1600/mean_large_unprojected.jpeg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-b1p62Zq23gk/U8lgMGSWXII/AAAAAAAAAQI/ag-CxRGgOcg/s1600/mean_large_unprojected.jpeg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792370478079000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gdsh7PsGUnNgUmPF0mL0Q\"><img src=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-b1p62Zq23gk/U8lgMGSWXII/AAAAAAAAAQI/ag-CxRGgOcg/s400/mean_large_unprojected.jpeg\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"296\"></a></p><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><div>Here&#39;s what the smaller data look like in a projected plot.</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">states_map</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   geom_polygon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;dark grey&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   coord_map</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">projection</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;mercator&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xlim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">125</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ylim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   coord_cartesian(xlim=c(-125, -100), ylim=c(30, 50)) +</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   geom_tile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mean_small</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   scale_fill_gradientn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">colours</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">brewer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;YlOrRd&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p</span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-WmVWlXM5TN8/U8leawSXY2I/AAAAAAAAAP8/gVkfKTkSEdQ/s1600/mean_small.jpeg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-WmVWlXM5TN8/U8leawSXY2I/AAAAAAAAAP8/gVkfKTkSEdQ/s1600/mean_small.jpeg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792370478079000&amp;usg=AOvVaw36C8iTXGPths9vSjYa0Jue\"><img src=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-WmVWlXM5TN8/U8leawSXY2I/AAAAAAAAAP8/gVkfKTkSEdQ/s400/mean_small.jpeg\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"296\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
